# VybeKiit maintainer patterns

Quick checklist for agents working on **this monorepo**. Full detail lives in `AGENTS.md`,
`CONTEXT.md`, and `docs/adr/`.

## Owned vs Maintained — where code goes

| Bucket | Path | Rule |
|---|---|---|
| **Maintained** | `packages/*` | Headless TS only. Published `@vybekiit/*`. Buyers never edit; updates = npm bumps. |
| **Owned** | `templates/*` | All UI + buyer agent layer. Copied into buyer repos; frozen after scaffold. |
| **Our app** | `apps/landing` | Marketing + gate logic. Not a buyer template. |
| **CLI** | `cli/` | Public scaffolder. No templates or secrets inside. |

Before adding code: logic the buyer shouldn't touch → `packages/`. UI, screens, copy → `templates/`.

## Provider pattern (every `@vybekiit/*` concern)

- One **interface** per concern (`PaymentProvider`, `DataProvider`, `AuthProvider`, …).
- Concrete backends live under `providers/<name>/`.
- One **default** adapter; others are opt-in via env (`PAYMENTS_PROVIDER`, `DATA_PROVIDER`, …).
- Env keys typed + Zod-validated in `@vybekiit/core`; root `.env.example` is SSOT for all keys.
- Adding an adapter never adds a buyer skill — skills target the interface once.

## Package rules (`packages/*`)

- Pure TypeScript. **No UI**, no framework lock.
- Strict TS: no `any`; narrow in `catch` (`instanceof Error`) before use.
- **JSDoc/TSDoc** on every export — document *why* and non-obvious constraints.
- Zod at public boundaries. No scattered URLs or secrets.
- Files ~200–400 lines; split when a file does multiple jobs.
- Match nearest sibling style; reuse helpers before writing new ones.

## TDD & quality gate

- **Tests first:** red → green → refactor. Green suite = safe `update-kit` for buyers.
- **Pre-commit:** lenient (format + lint-fix only) — must not block on failing tests.
- **CI / pre-push:** heavy gate (lint → typecheck → test → build).
- Run typecheck/test/lint after substantial changes.

## Editing buyer-facing content (`templates/*`)

When touching skills, `AGENTS.md`, `BUILDER-VOICE.md`, or `language.md` inside templates:

- **Decide + Guide** contract: one action at a time, verify-before-advance, plain language.
- Never use maintainer jargon ("env var", "deploy", "merge conflict") — translate per
  `templates/*/BUILDER-VOICE.md`.
- **No em dashes (`—`)** in buyer-facing copy. UI titles and section headings: no em dash, no trailing period or comma. See `language.md` → Tone.
- Skills are **goal-named** (`go-live`), never tech-named. Layer B platform-skills are agent-only.

## Workflow

- Trunk-based: squash-PR to `main` (no direct push to protected `main`).
- Never commit secrets. `.env.example` documents keys; `.env` stays local.
- Semver for `@vybekiit/*` publishes. Templates versioned but not npm-published.

## Pointers

- Blueprint & glossary → `CONTEXT.md`
- Maintainer agent rules → `AGENTS.md`
- Architecture decisions → `docs/adr/`
- Buyer template patterns → `templates/*/.cursor/rules/patterns.mdc` (different voice)
